      "urpx:forRatePlan": {
        "@id": "jemc:mbs"
      },
      "urpx:hasCoverageClaim": {
        "@id": "jemc:cc-mbs-2022-01-01",
        "@type": "urpx:CoverageClaim",
        "urpx:completenessResult": {
          "@id": "urpx:partial"
        },
        "urpx:selfContained": true,
        "urpx:explainedBy": {
          "@type": "urpx:Evaluation",
          "@id": "jemc:cc-mbs-2022-01-01-evaluation",
          "urpx:evaluationKind": {
            "@id": "urpx:coverageEvaluation"
          },
          "urpx:description": "This filing does not carry everything its source document states. 4 parts are deferred, listed here in the same words as the filing's tariff.toml [modeling].deferrals so the two records cannot drift. (1) Energy Charge and Facilities Charge. The Energy Charge's kWh, transmission, fixed cost recovery, substation and line loss charges are determined case by case, subject to market prices, availability, contract terms, load characteristics and type of service, and the Facilities Charge is one-twelfth of the annual allocated cost of serving the customer. Neither is published, so each is a PriceDefinition with no Price and a modeled bill carries nothing for them. (2) Margin Cost. The Margin Cost is 3.0 percent of the first $15,000 of TC = EC + FC, 2.5 percent of the next $35,000 and 2.0 percent over $50,000. A multiplier Price applies to Prices, and EC and FC have none; dollar blocks of a total are not a ServiceTiers ladder either. The JSON-LD defines it as a PriceDefinition with no Price, with its percentages in its name. (3) Availability and connected demand. The schedule is for customers over 900 kW of connected demand at a single point of delivery, available case by case at the Cooperative's sole discretion. The EligibilityRule carries non-residential customer kind; these conditions are in its description only. (4) Terms of Payment and Contract Period. The sheet adds a late fee and disconnection charges under the Service Rules and Regulations, makes all charges subject to applicable taxes, and sets the contract period in the Agreement for Electric Service. None is carried.",
          "urpx:evaluatedOn": "2026-10-18T00:00:00"
        }
      }
    }
  }
